WHAT THIS IS
  A command-line VRAM bar graph. The GPU-facing part is not written here: it is
  provided by nvidia-smi-clone-RE (https://github.com/zagg/nvidia-smi-clone-RE),
  a free and independent reimplementation of the NVIDIA management interface,
  recovered by observing the driver's own behaviour on the author's hardware.
  nvfree statically links that library's nvrm.c and fields.c.

WHAT IS NOT HERE
  No NVIDIA source code, binary, firmware, dump or trademarked asset is included
  or redistributed. Interface facts come from headers NVIDIA ships under MIT with
  its open kernel module and from observed program behaviour.

READ-ONLY GUARANTEE
  nvfree issues only GET/QUERY controls, plus the version handshake and
  ATTACH_IDS required to open a driver client. It never writes to the device:
  no power limit, no persistence change, no reset, no ECC configuration.

